{
  "id": "DrugBank_DB01262 - MONDO_17893",
  "verbalization": "Decitabine is a clinically established drug with a well-documented indication for Acute Myeloblastic Leukemia Without Maturation, a subset of acute myeloid leukemia (AML). This relationship is supported by its ability to inhibit DNA methyltransferases, a mechanism that has been shown to modulate gene expression in AML. The evidence suggests that Decitabine may be repurposed for Inherited Acute Myeloid Leukemia, as it is associated with a chain of indications that ultimately lead to this condition. The presence of a direct indication for Decitabine in Acute Myeloblastic Leukemia Without Maturation, which in turn is linked to Inherited Acute Myeloid Leukemia, indicates a potential mechanistic pathway involving epigenetic regulation. The integration of these pathways suggests that Decitabine may exert its effects through a shared epigenetic mechanism, potentially influencing the same molecular processes that drive the development of Inherited Acute Myeloid Leukemia. The evidence is supported by a consistent pattern of indications across different pathways, though the exact molecular mechanism linking Decitabine to Inherited Acute Myeloid Leukemia remains to be fully elucidated.",
